  "note": "gbOpen passes through each country UPSTREAM licence — this collection is MIXED-LICENCE with per-country attribution duties.",
  "adm0_features": 162,
  "_duty": "130 of the 162 countries carry a duty that travels with any redistribution of boundaries/world-adm0*.geojson; only 32 are duty-free. The 130 split TWO ways and the split matters more than the total: 65 are attribution-only, and 65 are SHARE-ALIKE CLASS (58 ODbL + 7 explicit ShareAlike), which can constrain how a derivative is licensed rather than merely how it is credited. See _duty_classes. This matters because the repo is intended to be given away: these obligations are not discharged by shipping the file. See data/boundaries/ATTRIBUTION, which references this table by path.",
  "_duty_classes": {
    "_why": "THREE CLASSES, NOT TWO — corrected 2026-09-28 after a review challenge, which was right. The first version gave only the 7 explicitly-named ShareAlike countries their own field on the reasoning that share-alike is a stronger duty than attribution. By that same reasoning the field should hold 65: Open Data Commons ODbL 1.0 is itself a SHARE-ALIKE licence for databases — alongside attribution it requires a Derivative Database be offered under ODbL, and it has a keep-open provision. Separating 7 from 58 buried exactly the thing the field existed to surface.",
    "_precedent": "THIS REPO ALREADY TREATS ODbL AS CONSEQUENTIAL, which is the evidence rather than a reading of the licence: library/scripts/posters/data/README.md:36-50 records that Natural Earth's 1:10m ROADS were requested and DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED because of an ODbL attribution obligation. Someone here dropped a dataset over this class of duty.",
    "_open": "NOT A LEGAL CONCLUSION. Whether a redistributed boundary file is a 'Derivative Database' under ODbL is exactly the clause a giveaway needs a real answer on, and nobody on this project is qualified to give it. Recorded here, and raised with the licensing items, so the question is visible rather than settled by omission.",
